From 16b881eb7166c0ae0e01afa529180e4e7af264bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:30:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Modulate the fODF by anisotropy to suppress noisy GM and
 CSF

The SMI fODF is stored with p_00 = 1, so it integrates to 1 in every voxel
and its isotropic floor is a fixed 1/(4*pi) = 0.0796. MRtrix's default iFOD2
-cutoff is 0.05, so an unmodulated SMI fODF passes the termination test
everywhere in the brain, CSF included: 100% of simulated GM and CSF voxels
survive it. Density weighting by orientational coherence restores the
amplitude information the normalization removed.

Adds SMI.fODF_ModulationWeight (per voxel weight in [0,1]) and
SMI.modulate_fODF (applies it, returning SH coefficients including the l=0
term that out.plm does not store), plus grab_pl/grab_kernel_pl accessors.
Additions only; existing code paths are untouched, so fits without
modulation are bit-identical.

Measured on a 7 class simulation at SNR 30 and 15, with and without the
regularized deconvolution (example_fODF_modulation.m,
REPORT_fODF_modulation.md):

- The default weight is the product of the two independent p2 estimates,
  out.kernel(p2) .* out.pl(:,:,:,1). They fail in opposite ways. The kernel
  p2 does not fall to 0 in CSF (median 0.31 against a true 0) because its
  polynomial regression returns roughly the prior mean where the l=2 signal
  is uninformative; alone it leaves 54-80% of CSF above cutoff. The
  deconvolved pl2 is unbiased but has a noise tail; alone it leaves 20-41%
  at SNR 15. The product reaches 0% in three of four conditions.

- p4 is rejected in both flavours. The kernel p4 carries the same upward
  bias, and the deconvolved pl4 is damped far harder than l=2 by the
  Tikhonov term (0.26 in single fibre WM against a true 0.71), so weighting
  by it leaves 84% of CSF above cutoff, worse than not weighting at all.

- Anisotropy weights preserve edema where tissue fraction weights do not.
  Under the cutoff retaining 95% of white matter, the simulated edema class
  is kept 100% by every p2 weight, but only 94% by f and 85% by 1-fw.

- Modulation does not substitute for regularization. At SNR 15 the
  unregularized deconvolution produced CSF peaks up to 2.2e14, reproducing
  the amplitudes seen in real data; the regularized fit caps the same voxels
  at 0.45. The weight is clipped at 1, so it cannot rescue a blown-up voxel.

Helpers live in fODF_modulation_helpers.m rather than as local functions at
the end of the example, because MATLAB requires local functions at the end
of a script while Octave cannot call them there, and this keeps the example
runnable and testable outside MATLAB.

