From 2ffbcd6fc86d6050555fabe1e2477f118b30ff18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 17:27:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Make the fODF modulation a toggleable flag on SMI.fit

Adds options.fODF_modulation.flag_modulate, off by default, mirroring how
options.fODF_regularization is already plumbed through. This lets the same
script be run with and without the modulation.

The modulation is applied after the deconvolution has finished, so it stays
downstream of the non-negativity constraint, which operates on the
normalized fODF. out.plm, out.pl and out.kernel are bit-identical whether
the flag is on or off (verified, max difference exactly 0); the modulated
fODF is returned separately as out.fODF_modulated, and the weight map and
degenerate voxel count as out.fODF_modulation. Flipping the flag therefore
cannot perturb anything upstream, and the two runs differ only by the added
output. Settings are written to the log file, including an explicit
"none" line when the flag is off, so a log identifies which way a run was
done.

SMI.fODF_ModulationDefaults validates the options, and the fit rejects
flag_modulate = 1 with flag_fit_fODF = 0 rather than silently doing
nothing. A numeric source is logged as "user supplied map" instead of
printing the array. Voxels outside the mask come back as 0 rather than the
NaN of out.plm, since a NaN breaks downstream tractography; this is
documented at both the method and the option.

Still additions only to existing code paths, so a fit that does not mention
fODF_modulation is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QW525oRotCnn6M4gCmS8cP
---
